<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                           revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>ShotIt</displayName>
  <description>Policies for the ShotIt screenshot tool</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="ShotIt">ShotIt</string>

      <string id="DisableUpload">Turn off uploading</string>
      <string id="DisableUpload_Help">When enabled, ShotIt cannot send a screenshot over the network: Upload, the upload test in Settings and Search image on the web are all blocked, and the Upload page in Settings says so.

When disabled or not configured, users can set up an upload destination and upload screenshots they choose to upload. ShotIt never uploads anything on its own.</string>

      <string id="DisableHistory">Turn off history</string>
      <string id="DisableHistory_Help">When enabled, ShotIt keeps no record of captures: no history entries, no internal copies and no stored text. Copying and saving still work.

When disabled or not configured, users choose in Settings what is kept. History is always stored only in the user's own profile on this computer.</string>

      <string id="DisableUpdates">Turn off automatic updates</string>
      <string id="DisableUpdates_Help">When enabled, ShotIt never checks for, downloads or installs updates. Use this when new versions are deployed centrally.

Copies installed with the MSI package have this turned on by default.</string>

      <string id="UpdateFeedUrl">Update address</string>
      <string id="UpdateFeedUrl_Help">Replaces the built-in address ShotIt downloads updates from, for organisations that host approved releases internally. The address must start with https://.

This has no effect when automatic updates are turned off.</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="UpdateFeedUrl">
        <textBox refId="UpdateFeedUrl">
          <label>Address (https://…)</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
